      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHOOPS A DAISY (5) brings the most persuasive recent profile, with consecutive BM64 efforts where she was beaten just under three lengths and now comes back to a BM56. The Morphettville sixth behind Sensational Secret had merit after she made ground, and Rochelle Milnes going back on is another plus. Can give this a shake. ATOMIC TIME (1) is the main danger if the shorter trip sparks him; his last-start Strathalbyn tenth was plain, but his broader season has been sound and Harry Grace has already won on him. Can bounce back. COSMIC INTERLUDE (3) resumes off two trials and has a win and a placing from four runs around 1100m, so she can be sharper than her late-campaign figures read. PRANCETHRULIFE (2) has a genuine track-and-trip reference and a recent trial third to build from, though he has to rebound from a heavy-track Morphettville failure before the break. In the mix.",
